### Soyuz UI strings (en-US source): tui-search
### The terminal UI: the search bar and its status row (Phase T5).
### Keys: <area>-<thing>, kebab-case. Keep keys identical in tr-TR/tui-search.ftl.

## The "save this search" dialog (Ctrl+S in the bar)

tui-search-save-name = Name
tui-search-save-name-empty = Give the search a name.
tui-search-save-body = Saved searches are listed in the sidebar under Searches; running one fills the bar again.
tui-search-save-hints = Enter save · Esc cancel

## The size filter dialog (the Size pill)

tui-search-size-body = Sizes like 512k, 10M or 1.5 GB. Leave a field empty for no limit.
tui-search-size-hints = Tab next · ←/→ preset · Enter apply · Esc cancel
tui-search-size-preset = Preset
tui-search-size-custom = Custom
tui-search-size-preset-tiny = < 16 KB
tui-search-size-preset-large = > 100 MB
tui-search-size-preset-huge = > 1 GB
# $value: what was typed.
tui-search-size-invalid = “{ $value }” is not a size (try 512k, 10M or 1.5 GB).

## The status line's key hint while the bar has the keyboard

tui-search-hint-field = Enter search · Tab next · ↓ results · Ctrl+S save · Esc close
tui-search-hint-controls = Space toggle · ←/→ move · Tab next · ↓ results · Esc close
